# Depth and computational omissions are explicit: an accessible paper is not a complete proof review.
notes={
345095:('parked','Source §2 fractional packing definition and §5 Conjecture 5.1 read; 200 structured LP diagnostics.','The source counts packing size as THREE times sum of triangle weights. Tested 40 near-complete-balanced-bipartite modifications at each n=26,27,28,32,40, seed 108, adding floor(n/8)+1 through floor(n/8)+8 internal edges and deleting 0 through 40 cross edges. All LP eta values exceed 1/4. Floating LPs are diagnostics, not certified infeasibility or optimality proofs.','Need a general stability inequality or an exact graph with eta≤1/4 and both bipartization numbers >n/8. No uniform dual certificate extracted.','outputs/near-bipartite.json'),
346161:('parked','Source §2 generating function, Corollary 12 and Conjecture 13/Remark 14 read; exact parity diagnostic.','Product of factors 1+q^k/(1-q^(2k)) evaluated modulo 2 through n=50000. This only measures a finite prefix and cannot decide the claimed limiting density. The source reduces the progression to parity of f3^8/f1^3, not a density theorem.','Need existence and value of a limiting parity density; no finite exception refutes a density limit.','logs/partitions50000.log'),
346664:('excluded_routine_bridge','Source §3.4, Proposition 2.2 and the proof discussion in §5 read.','Adjacent Boolean layers n-1 and n have V=C(m,n-1)+C(m,n), E=n C(m,n). They have no triangles or 4-cycles: two distinct n-subsets have at most one common (n-1)-subset. The graph is connected for 1≤n≤m+1, by exchanging leaves through the center. Source Proposition 2.2 attaches 2-cells only to triangles and chordless squares, hence A1 is the ordinary graph fundamental group, free of rank E-V+1, exactly the displayed expression. A1 is a fundamental group, not literally first homology as the raw paraphrase says.','No new credit: every substantive ingredient is in the source plus the classical graph fundamental-group rank formula. No Lean investment or exhaustive search needed after this bridge.','sources/2005.13557.txt'),
347264:('parked','Source algorithm sections, order-24 results and §5 Conjecture 5.1 read; fixed-matrix exact diagnostics.','Constructed Paley H24 from F23 and H40=H2 tensor Paley H20 from F19, verified H^T H=nI exactly. Tested all 4096 circulant connection subsets at order 24 and all 1351 subsets with at most 3 positive jumps at order 40 against these fixed matrices. These are labelled circulants, not isomorphism classes or all graphs diagonalized by all Hadamard matrices.','Need at least 27 non-isomorphic examples at a single allowed order, or structural classification. Neither fixed-matrix sample counts nor the order-32 family settle allowed orders.','outputs/hadamard.json'),
347432:('parked_definition_reconstruction_gap','Source §4.2 Construction A, proof of Theorem 1.3, and Conjecture 5.1 read.','Source distinguishes original binary codes C_M from fourfold expanded codes Ctilde_M. Theorem 1.3 proves non-isomorphism only for the expanded lattices, so it does not close the conjecture about original lattices. Graph pair starts from Figure 1, joins P_n and subdivides six distinguished edges; length is 3m+11n+24. Figure graph incidence matrices were not recovered into a validated executable model; no lattice isometry search run.','Need exact Figure 1 edge lists, code construction convention, and an invariant distinguishing the two original Construction A lattices. Original-code inequivalence alone does not automatically imply lattice non-isometry.','sources/2007.15089.txt'),
347914:('excluded_published_resolution','Source Conjectures 4.5/4.6; Perian-Xu-Zhang arXiv:2008.02380 Theorem 1 and its reduction/induction proof read.','Theorem 1 is exactly (n^3+6n^2-55n+54)/6 for n≥7. Proof reduces to n+1 classes with neither leading n nor trailing 1, then reconstructs the recurrence. Journal of Integer Sequences publication dated October 17, 2020. Ma primary PRIMES paper predates its 2020 arXiv posting.','Known full-scope enumeration; no new credit and no new enumeration investment.','sources/2008.02380.txt'),
350724:('parked','Source root-subsystem discussion and §3.3 Conjecture 3.2 read; exact reduced-word graph searches.','All permutations S3,S4,S5 (6,24,120) and all 461 permutations in S6 with inversion number ≤8. Enumerated every reduced word, all commutation and braid edges, and BFS from every word to compute exact diameters. L2 counts disjoint inversion pairs plus decreasing triples; 3412 occurrences counted directly. All bounds pass. Largest fully tested graph has 768 vertices (S5 longest word), diameter 25.','Need uniform routing improvement removing one rank-two contribution per 3412 occurrence, or a larger witness. Source does not specify a numeric verified range for this conjecture, so no beyond-range claim.','outputs/reduced.json'),
350890:('parked','Source Theorem 17, Conjecture 18 and circulant definitions read; exact bounded label searches.','Circ(n,k) has jumps ±1,±k. Found prime-distance labellings in [0,127], fixing vertex 0 label 0, for (n,k)=(15,4),(15,5),(15,6),(16,2),(16,4),(16,6),(17,4),(17,5),(17,6). All edge differences checked prime and all labels distinct. These parameters extend the authors n≤14 range.','Need uniform labelling or a nonexistence proof with unbounded integer labels. Finite label-window failure would not be such a proof.','outputs/prime-distance.json'),
350979:('candidate_full_lean_refutation_pending_root','Source Conjecture 4.5 and proof of Theorem 4.4/Lemma 4.3 read; survey arXiv:2501.19385 §4 repeats conjecture. Exhaustive order-15 search, independent elementary classifier, complete Lean semantics and fresh replay.','No circulant graph of order 15 has diameter 2 and monophonic position number 2. Of 128 symmetric jump sets, 109 contain a triangle, 17 have some vertex at distance >2 from 0, and 2 have three vertices 0,5,10 with identical open neighborhoods. A triangle is a monophonic set; three distinct twins are a monophonic set because any neighbor of one on an induced path would have to have three neighbors on that path. The two exceptions are masks 41 and 70. Additional searches were diagnostic only and are not needed for the theorem.','Independent statement-fidelity, novelty/significance and root acceptance remain. No source theorem read supplies the finite classification. Classical C5 blow-ups appear as residual objects, but the result is universal nonexistence over all circulants, not a boundary reinterpretation of one extremal graph. See CANDIDATE.md and replay/replay.json.','outputs/order15-certificate.json'),
351294:('parked','Source Definition 2.1, Proposition 2.3, flipped-game discussion and Conjecture 7.3 read; two exhaustive beyond-range searches.','All distinct ordered pairs at exact lengths 14 and 16, modulo simultaneous bit complement (134209536 and 2147450880 pairs). Exact Conway correlations and cross multiplication compare probabilities. Best restricted four-form response was never beaten; no outside tied optimum found. Source verified through 10. No claim of having independently checked every intervening length.','Need uniform domination inequality for all response strings, or an actual larger counterexample; finite correlation calculations are not a probability theorem.','logs/penney16.log'),
351778:('excluded_published_resolution','Source conjecture and Li-Xia-Zhou arXiv:2302.04022 Theorem 3.5 and Corollary 3.7 proof read.','Corollary 3.7 explicitly confirms Maleki-Razafimahatratra Conjecture 1.4. Its cycle length parameter is n-k in the reserved source notation; substitution gives exactly (k-1)/(n-1) C(n,k)(n-k-1)!. Cases n=4,5,6 handled separately, general case follows Theorem 3.5(a,d).','Known full-scope result; no new credit.','sources/2302.04022.txt'),
351914:('parked','Source §9.2, Theorem 9.2 proof and Conjecture 9.3 read; later arXiv:2306.07851 subgroup-scope comparison.','The later intersection-spectrum theorem proves existence of density 2 for q≡3 mod4 in a DIFFERENT coset action (cyclic point stabilizer), and Borel-subgroup results for q≡1 mod4. This does not by itself settle the dihedral point stabilizer of the 2-subset action. No new exact maximum-intersecting-set search run; no general-purpose finite-field/group package installed.','Need bounds for the actual 2-subset derangement graph, especially q≡1 mod4. Later abstract is not full-scope clearance; no new resolution asserted.','sources/2306.07851.txt'),
352087:('excluded_public_counterexample','Source invariant, Theorems 1.1/1.2 and Conjecture 1.3 read; public ProbXiv counterexample body independently checked.','Public construction dated August 17, 2026: V=F2^4=U⊕<z>, L=GL(3,2), G=V semidirect L; W=<z+a,z+b>. On W-cosets the conjugate planes are 21 spaces W_c,d. Exactly 13 meet W nontrivially, giving I=13/21>1/2. Then q=21/5, 2q not integral. Exhaustively checked the 21 planes and 13 intersections. This is prior public work, not our discovery.','No new credit. Public model review labels are not proof authority; the explicit subspace count and coset-index argument are the supporting mathematics.','outputs/suborbit-prior-check.json'),
352332:('parked','Source generating function (1.1), eventual asymptotic theorem and exact-threshold conjecture read; exact coefficient computations.','For each k=2,...,30, computed Nk(m,n)-Nk(m+1,n) from the alternating false-theta series times partition numbers, for all n_u(k)≤n≤1200 and 0≤m<n-k. Every tested adjacent comparison is nonnegative. Source k≤10,n≤1000 range is extended in both directions. Python integer arithmetic and object arrays, no floating rounding.','Need an effective uniform small-threshold argument. Eventual unimodality theorem alone leaves unbounded k and a non-explicit cutoff. No uniform LP certificate found.','outputs/garvan.json'),
353076:('parked_definition_model_gap','Source Conjecture 7.2, split/join pattern definition and cover enumerator discussion read; journal search locates same conjecture as 79 in 2024 version.','Type-B composition here is join (t>0). Ordinary type-B Narayana numbers at t=0 are a proved different family. No source-faithful enumeration of the join-case parabolic avoiders and their covers was implemented; no numerical coverage claimed.','Need a validated signed-permutation avoidance/cover model before search. Vandermonde proves the consequent cardinality from the proposed polynomial but not the proposed polynomial itself.','sources/2112.13400.txt'),
353079:('parked_sustained_exact_recurrence','Source Conjecture 12, Corollary 11 proof and Theorem 13 mechanism read; dense and very large-index exact computations.','Let A(z),B(z) enumerate evil/odious numbers. A=A(z²)+zB(z²), B=B(z²)+zA(z²). Expanded all seven mixed products A^j B^(6-j). Checked every coefficient difference through n=2000000 using signed 128-bit arithmetic (total coefficients bounded by C(n+5,5), far below 2^127). Last failures: r6 at 36, s6 at 4. Independent memoized arbitrary-integer recurrence checked 196 or 202 explicit sparse points near/randomly between 2^k and 2^(k+1), k=10,20,50,100,200,500; no failures.','Need a uniform invariant cone or signed-matrix positivity certificate. Source analytic alpha=log3/log4 method requires at least 10 summands, so does not prove 6. An initial sparse run hit Python recursion depth; corrected run retained separately.','outputs/thue-sparse.json'),
356821:('parked','Source definitions and Theorems 7-10/Conjecture 11 vicinity read; current public search did not identify a full resolution.','The conjecture is an infinite coloring/avoidance problem, not a bounded arithmetic identity. Source SAT bounds >8000 and >100000 are lower bounds, not exact nonexistence claims. No new SAT coloring search beyond these bounds was run after the finite circulant candidate emerged.','Need a uniform coloring construction or a finite UNSAT certificate at an admissible parameter, with source difference-sequence semantics. No asymptotic or open-label inference.','sources/2211.05167.txt'),
381803:('parked_asymptotic','Source Theorem 3.1 and Conjecture 3.3/Table 3 read.','Source exhausts unlabeled trees through order 20. A finite counterexample at one order cannot refute a limiting-proportion assertion. A plausible route is a positive-density pendant-limb pattern forcing linearly many eigenvalues <1, while typical tree diameter is sublinear; this requires actual random-unlabeled-tree pattern and diameter theorems. No fresh tree enumeration run and no claims beyond the source range.','Need exact asymptotic counting/model (unlabeled versus labelled) and a spectral limb lemma; neither a numerical inertia count nor source Table 3 supplies the limit.','sources/2212.05283.txt'),
381896:('parked_source_internal_coefficient_conflict','Source rank/tableau definition, HPC procedure, Table 1 and Conjecture 3.1 read.','Introduction displays coefficient 52 C(n,12) in N3,n,4, but Conjecture 3.1 has 48 C(n,12), as does MathDB. At n=12, Table 1 reports 92980, while 288 C(12,9)+400 C(12,10)+264 C(12,11)+48=92976; using 52 gives 92980. This source-internal inconsistency is a zero-credit correction, not a novel counterexample. No new cluster mutation search run (source reports ~0.5 million CPU hours).','Need authors dataset/version adjudication and an intended-coefficient full theorem. Do not formalize a table-versus-formula discrepancy for credit.','sources/2212.09771.txt'),
381902:('parked_literal_defect_intended_search_pass','Source Theorem 1.3 definition of signed inverse, Conjecture 3 and Corollary 3.2 read; original and corrected parity searches.','Raw says inverse modulo p²; source uses inverse modulo p, chosen negative with 1≤-inverse≤p-1. Literal p² version has failures even of the source total-parity theorem (e.g. p=79,n=1,alpha=0 gives index 520). This is not eligible credit. Reran intended signed-inverse progressions for all p≤1000 in P with p≡1,7 mod24 and all resulting nonnegative indices≤50000; see output for exact coverage/failures.','Need uniform mod-4 congruence b3(m)=q(S2;m) for the source progressions, or an intended-scope counterexample. The source itself proposes this route; no uniform certificate derived.','outputs/progression-source.json')}
